# Every text file is LF in the repository AND in the working copy.
#
# Without this, a machine with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) gets CRLF written into the
# working copy on every checkout, and the token gate's "keeps every source file on LF" rule goes red
# on a tree nobody touched. It happened on 2026-08-04: a `git reset --hard` rewrote 27 restored files
# as CRLF and the gate failed. `eol=lf` is what makes the checkout side match the storage side, so
# the rule holds for a fresh clone as well as an edited tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never translate.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
